{
  "id": "task-diy-5",
  "task": 5,
  "title": "DIY 5, step by step",
  "segments": [
    {
      "example": null,
      "extra": false,
      "title": "A String never changes, and literals are shared",
      "steps": [
        {
          "caption": "original points at the literal Hello in the string pool. The tag shows the object's identity number: a number that belongs to that object alone.",
          "vars": [{"name": "original", "ref": "H"}],
          "arrays": [{"id": "H", "text": "Hello", "class": "String #4821", "pool": true}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Store that number in an int before touching anything: 4821 here. The real number is longer and changes from run to run, which is why the program prints only comparisons.",
          "vars": [{"name": "original", "ref": "H"}, {"name": "before", "value": "4821"}],
          "arrays": [{"id": "H", "text": "Hello", "class": "String #4821", "pool": true}],
          "flow": [{"from": {"array": "H"}, "to": {"var": "before"}, "text": "4821"}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Add World to the end and store the result back in original. A String can never change, so a brand-new String is built, and original's arrow moves to it.",
          "vars": [{"name": "original", "ref": "HW"}, {"name": "before", "value": "4821"}],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "H", "text": "Hello", "class": "String #4821", "pool": true},
            {"id": "W", "text": " World", "class": "String", "pool": true},
            {"id": "HW", "text": "Hello World", "class": "String #7306"}
          ],
          "flow": [
            {"from": {"array": "H", "index": 0}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 0}, "text": "H"},
            {"from": {"array": "H", "index": 1}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 1}, "text": "e"},
            {"from": {"array": "H", "index": 2}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 2}, "text": "l"},
            {"from": {"array": "H", "index": 3}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 3}, "text": "l"},
            {"from": {"array": "H", "index": 4}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 4}, "text": "o"},
            {"from": {"array": "W", "index": 0}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 5}, "text": "␣"},
            {"from": {"array": "W", "index": 1}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 6}, "text": "W"},
            {"from": {"array": "W", "index": 2}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 7}, "text": "o"},
            {"from": {"array": "W", "index": 3}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 8}, "text": "r"},
            {"from": {"array": "W", "index": 4}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 9}, "text": "l"},
            {"from": {"array": "W", "index": 5}, "to": {"array": "HW", "index": 10}, "text": "d"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Its identity number is 7306: a different object, so the two numbers are not equal.",
          "print": "Same object after concat? false\n",
          "vars": [
            {"name": "original", "ref": "HW"},
            {"name": "before", "value": "4821"},
            {"name": "after", "value": "7306"}
          ],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "H", "text": "Hello", "class": "String #4821", "pool": true},
            {"id": "W", "text": " World", "class": "String", "pool": true},
            {"id": "HW", "text": "Hello World", "class": "String #7306"}
          ],
          "compare": [{"a": {"var": "before"}, "b": {"var": "after"}, "same": false}],
          "flow": [{"from": {"array": "HW"}, "to": {"var": "after"}, "text": "7306"}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "The text is now Hello World. The old Hello is still in the pool, unchanged.",
          "print": "Text now: Hello World\n",
          "from": {"array": "HW"},
          "vars": [
            {"name": "original", "ref": "HW"},
            {"name": "before", "value": "4821"},
            {"name": "after", "value": "7306"}
          ],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "H", "text": "Hello", "class": "String #4821", "pool": true, "note": "unchanged"},
            {"id": "W", "text": " World", "class": "String", "pool": true},
            {"id": "HW", "text": "Hello World", "class": "String #7306"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Two variables given the same literal, Lab. The pool keeps one copy: two arrows, one object.",
          "vars": [{"name": "lit1", "ref": "L"}, {"name": "lit2", "ref": "L"}],
          "arrays": [{"id": "L", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "pool": true, "color": "blue"}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Compare the arrows, not the text: they lead to the same object, so true.",
          "print": "Two literals are the same object? true\n",
          "vars": [{"name": "lit1", "ref": "L"}, {"name": "lit2", "ref": "L"}],
          "arrays": [{"id": "L", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "pool": true, "color": "blue"}],
          "compare": [{"a": {"var": "lit1"}, "b": {"var": "lit2"}, "same": true}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "heap1 and heap2 are each made with new. That always builds a fresh object outside the pool, even when the pool already holds Lab.",
          "vars": [
            {"name": "lit1", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "lit2", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "heap1", "ref": "N1"},
            {"name": "heap2", "ref": "N2"}
          ],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "L", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "pool": true, "color": "blue"},
            {"id": "N1", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "pink"},
            {"id": "N2", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "purple"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Two different objects, so their arrows differ: false.",
          "print": "Two new Strings are the same object? false\n",
          "vars": [
            {"name": "lit1", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "lit2", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "heap1", "ref": "N1"},
            {"name": "heap2", "ref": "N2"}
          ],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "L", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "pool": true, "color": "blue"},
            {"id": "N1", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "pink"},
            {"id": "N2", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "purple"}
          ],
          "compare": [{"a": {"var": "heap1"}, "b": {"var": "heap2"}, "same": false}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "A new object against the pooled one: false again, although the text is the same.",
          "print": "A new String is the pooled object? false\n",
          "vars": [
            {"name": "lit1", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "lit2", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "heap1", "ref": "N1"},
            {"name": "heap2", "ref": "N2"}
          ],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "L", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "pool": true, "color": "blue"},
            {"id": "N1", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "pink"},
            {"id": "N2", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "purple"}
          ],
          "compare": [{"a": {"var": "heap1"}, "b": {"var": "lit1"}, "same": false}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Ask heap1's String for its pooled copy: intern hands back an arrow to the pool's Lab. heap1 itself does not change.",
          "vars": [
            {"name": "lit1", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "lit2", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "heap1", "ref": "N1"},
            {"name": "heap2", "ref": "N2"},
            {"name": "intern()", "ref": "L"}
          ],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "L", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "pool": true, "color": "blue"},
            {"id": "N1", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "pink"},
            {"id": "N2", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "purple"}
          ],
          "flow": [{"from": {"array": "N1"}, "to": {"array": "L"}, "text": "Lab"}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "That arrow and lit1 lead to the same object: true.",
          "print": "intern() returns the pooled object? true\n",
          "vars": [
            {"name": "lit1", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "lit2", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "heap1", "ref": "N1"},
            {"name": "heap2", "ref": "N2"},
            {"name": "intern()", "ref": "L"}
          ],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "L", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "pool": true, "color": "blue"},
            {"id": "N1", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "pink"},
            {"id": "N2", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "purple"}
          ],
          "compare": [{"a": {"var": "intern()"}, "b": {"var": "lit1"}, "same": true}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Now write the code that makes this happen, run it with ▶, then press Check my output.",
          "vars": [
            {"name": "lit1", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "lit2", "ref": "L"},
            {"name": "heap1", "ref": "N1"},
            {"name": "heap2", "ref": "N2"},
            {"name": "intern()", "ref": "L"}
          ],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "L", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "pool": true, "color": "blue"},
            {"id": "N1", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "pink"},
            {"id": "N2", "text": "Lab", "class": "String", "color": "purple"}
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
